  "notes": "Xiaomi MiTV-AXSO0 (codename dangal; sold as Mi TV 4C Pro 2019 and Mi TV 4A Pro), Android TV 9 (SDK 28),\nfirmware PI.6036, Amlogic/droidlogic.\nLive TV app: com.android.tv (set it as live_tv_package and hide it in launcher config.xml).\nStock launcher: com.google.android.tvlauncher (the default, disabled by build-and-install.sh).\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/xiaomi-mitv-axso0/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/xiaomi-mitv-axso0/debloat.txt\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nNotes from this firmware:\n- Default IME is already Gboard, so the Mi TV 4A missing-keyboard quirk doesn't apply.\n- `svc power reboot` gets killed; reboot through adb's own reboot service instead.\n- com.google.android.leanbacklauncher is re-enabled by the firmware at every boot, so it's not listed.\n- Glance (com.glance.tv) puts news and ads on the lock/standby screen; with it off the screensaver is clean.\n- Netflix, Prime Video and YouTube are preinstalled system apps, so they always get BOOT_COMPLETED.\nOther apps stay out of the boot-time rush after `am force-stop`, until someone opens them again.\nXiaomi + Google telemetry",
